From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Widen license-files to cover vendored dependency licences

pyproject.toml declares the PEP 639 license-files = [ "LICENSE" ] as an
explicit list, so scikit-build-core's default LICEN[CS]E*/COPYING*/
NOTICE*/AUTHORS* glob never runs and only that one path is ever
collected. The extension statically compiles in Eigen (MPL2, plus
BSD/LGPL components), voro++ (BSD-ish) and fsph (MIT) from their git
submodules, plus the vendored extern/bessel-library.hpp header (MIT);
nanobind (BSD-3-Clause, a pip build dependency) vendors tsl::robin_map
(MIT); and oneTBB (Apache-2.0) is built from source and dynamically
linked in by the workflow's before-build step. None of those licences
ship in upstream's own wheel; verified against the real
freud_analysis-3.6.1 wheels on PyPI, which have the same gap.

Widening the explicit list to also match LICENSE.* lets the build add
LICENSE.eigen/LICENSE.voropp/LICENSE.fsph/LICENSE.bessel-library/
LICENSE.nanobind/LICENSE.robin-map/LICENSE.tbb at the project root with
no other packaging change, and removes the conflict scikit-build-core
otherwise raises (AssertionError: Both project.license-files and
tool.scikit-build.wheel.license-files are set) against this
workflow's own SKBUILD_WHEEL_LICENSE_FILES, which is now redundant and
is dropped in the same change.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; this port may only touch riseproject-dev/python-wheels]
---
 pyproject.toml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
index 0848fdc..83c861f 100644
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@ requires-python = ">=3.12"
 description = "Powerful, efficient trajectory analysis in scientific Python."
 readme = "README.rst"
 license = "BSD-3-Clause"
-license-files = [ "LICENSE" ]
+license-files = [ "LICENSE", "LICENSE.*" ]
 authors = [
     { name = "The Glotzer Lab" }
 ]
